.TH VDR-SUITE-FIRST-ADMIN-SETUP 8 "October 2026" "VDR-Suite" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-first-admin-setup \- interactively create the first VDR-Suite administrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-first-admin-setup
.RI [ --database " PATH" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdr-suite-first-admin-setup
is a local, root-only interactive setup command for an unclaimed VDR-Suite
server. It requires an interactive terminal. It asks for a login name, display
name, and a new password twice with terminal echo disabled.
.PP
The command uses the existing short-lived first-admin bootstrap issuance
service and the existing atomic first-admin claim service locally, against
the same Suite SQLite database. It does not send credentials over HTTP,
print the setup secret or password, create any new security authority, or
install a separate service.
.PP
It refuses to create another first administrator if the server is already
claimed. If an earlier short-lived bootstrap issuance is still active, it
also refuses to issue a competing proof. Allow that authorization to expire
before retrying; do not delete or recreate the SQLite database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --database " PATH"
Use an explicit absolute path to a VDR-Suite database. The default is
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db .
.SH SECURITY
The operator must be root and have a trusted interactive terminal.
Passwords require a minimum of 12 characters. The command does not
accept a password on the command line or through standard input pipes.
It does not change existing accounts, login credentials, or session grants.
.PP
The local claim produces the same first-admin audit event and administrator
grant as the established HTTP claim route.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on successful first-admin creation, 64 on invalid input,
74 on storage or authorization failure, 77 on permission or claim-state
protection failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db
Default Suite security database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-first-admin-bootstrap (8),
.BR vdr-suite-human-account-recover (8),
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
